v 3
d datalib. Survey microdata as a versioned asset (IHSN-organized archive)
d Version 1.7.0
d
d Commands to read (datalib), deposit (_dtlb_put) and validate (_dtlb_check)
d survey microdata organized in the datalib / IHSN folder taxonomy, plus the
d IBGE import pipeline (ibge) and a vendored YAML parser used by the registry.
d
d Modules declare their own structure -- unit of observation, keys and parent --
d in module_schema: in datalib.yaml, mirrored into dataset characteristics, so
d a multi-module load is planned from the data rather than from a hardcoded
d table (_dtlb_modspec, _dtlb_mergeplan). datalib_whence reports the provenance
d a dataset carries about itself.
d See 00_documentation/taxonomy.md for the shared specification (the same
d contract is implemented by the Python and R datalib packages).
d
d Requires: Stata 16+ (the catalog uses frames; _dtlb_catalog,
d _dtlb_catalogregistry and _dtlb_ipums_extract declare version 16)
d
d NOTE ON DIRECTIVES: lowercase "f" installs only extensions Stata
d recognises (.ado .sthlp .scheme .style); anything else -- .yaml
d included -- is SILENTLY DROPPED while net install still returns 0.
d Capital "F" ships the file regardless of extension. That is why
d src/registry/catalogs.yaml below uses F. Same approach as
d wbopendata.pkg, which ships its four _wbopendata_*.yaml with F.
d
d Authors: Joao Pedro Azevedo (UNICEF), Minh Cong Nguyen (World Bank)
d Support: jpazevedo@unicef.org
d
